/// `arima_fit(x, p, d, q)`: `list(ar, ma, sigma2, aic, loglik, mean)` of an
/// ARIMA(`p`, `d`, `q`) fitted by Hannan–Rissanen and refined by conditional
/// sum of squares. Fits an ARIMA(`p`, `d`, `q`) model. The series is
/// differenced `d` times and an ARMA(`p`, `q`) is fitted to the result by the
/// Hannan–Rissanen procedure: a long autoregression provides residuals, a
/// regression on lagged values and lagged residuals gives initial parameters,
/// and a Gauss–Newton search on the conditional sum of squares refines them.
/// Orders are capped at `p ≤ 6` and `q ≤ 4`. # Errors Returns a lowercase
/// message when an order exceeds the cap, the series is too short for the
/// requested differencing or order, or a least-squares stage cannot be solved.
inline Term arima_fit(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                      const Term &a3) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3};
  return apply("arima_fit", args, 4);
}

/// `arima_forecast(x, p, d, q, horizon)`: the next `horizon` values of `x`
/// under an ARIMA(`p`, `d`, `q`) refitted to the whole series. Forecasts an
/// ARIMA model forward from a series. `x` must be the series the model was
/// fitted to, i.e. already differenced `d` times, so the returned values are
/// forecasts of the same differenced series. Future shocks are set to zero, so
/// the forecasts follow the conditional mean recursion. # Errors Returns a
/// lowercase message when the horizon is zero and the series is empty, or the
/// series is shorter than the model order.
inline Term arima_forecast(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                           const Term &a3, const Term &a4) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4};
  return apply("arima_forecast", args, 5);
}

