/// `dwt2(matrix, wavelet)`: single-level 2D separable discrete wavelet
/// transform returning `list(LL, LH, HL, HH)`. The first letter gives the
/// row-wise filter and the second gives the column-wise filter. One level of
/// the separable two-dimensional transform, `x` row-major with `rows x cols`
/// entries. The rows are transformed first, then the columns, and the four
/// sub-bands are packed into a `(2*ra) x (2*ca)` row-major array with `ra =
/// w.coeff_len(rows, b)` and `ca = w.coeff_len(cols, b)`: `LL` at rows `0..ra`,
/// columns `0..ca`; `LH` at rows `0..ra`, columns `ca..2ca`; `HL` at rows
/// `ra..2ra`, columns `0..ca`; `HH` at rows `ra..2ra`, columns `ca..2ca`. In
/// each label, the first letter gives the filter within each row (horizontal)
/// and the second the filter within each column (vertical). # Errors
/// [`WaveletError::Shape`] when `rows * cols` does not match `x.len()`, or when
/// a row or column transform fails.
inline Term dwt2(const Term &a0, const Term &a1) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1};
  return apply("dwt2", args, 2);
}

