/// `glm_fit(x, y, family, link, weights, tol)`: `list(beta, se, deviance,
/// null_deviance, aic, iterations, fitted)` of a generalised linear model
/// fitted by iteratively reweighted least squares; `x` is a list of rows
/// without an intercept, `weights` is empty for equal weights. Fits a
/// generalised linear model by iteratively reweighted least squares. `x` holds
/// one row of covariates per observation and must **not** contain an intercept
/// column; `fit` prepends one, so the returned coefficient vector has
/// `x[0].len() + 1` entries with the intercept first. `weights` are prior
/// weights (number of trials for a binomial proportion, exposure for a Poisson
/// rate); when `None` every observation weighs one. Convergence is declared
/// when `max |Δβ| / (1 + |β|) < tol`. Each step is halved up to `MAX_HALVINGS`
/// times while the deviance would increase. # Errors Returns a lowercase
/// message when the design and response disagree in length, the design is empty
/// or non-finite, a weight is not strictly positive, the response leaves the
/// family's support, `max_iter` is zero, `tol` is not positive, there are fewer
/// observations than parameters, or a linear system in the iteration is
/// singular.
inline Term glm_fit(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                    const Term &a3, const Term &a4, const Term &a5) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5};
  return apply("glm_fit", args, 6);
}

