/// `holt_winters(x, season, alpha, beta, gamma)`: `list(fitted, level, trend,
/// season, sse)` of additive Holt–Winters smoothing. Holt–Winters smoothing
/// with an additive seasonal component. The recursion is `l_t = α(y_t -
/// s_{t-m}) + (1-α)(l_{t-1} + b_{t-1})`, `b_t = β(l_t - l_{t-1}) +
/// (1-β)b_{t-1}` and `s_t = γ(y_t - l_{t-1} - b_{t-1}) + (1-γ)s_{t-m}`, with
/// the first two seasons used for the starting values. # Errors Returns a
/// lowercase message when the seasonal period is zero, the series covers fewer
/// than two seasons, a value is not finite, or a smoothing parameter leaves
/// `[0, 1]`.
inline Term holt_winters(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                         const Term &a3, const Term &a4) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4};
  return apply("holt_winters", args, 5);
}

/// `holt_winters_mul(x, season, alpha, beta, gamma)`: the multiplicative
/// Holt–Winters form, `list(fitted, level, trend, season, sse)`. Holt–Winters
/// smoothing with a multiplicative seasonal component. The recursion is `l_t =
/// α(y_t / s_{t-m}) + (1-α)(l_{t-1} + b_{t-1})`, `b_t = β(l_t - l_{t-1}) +
/// (1-β)b_{t-1}` and `s_t = γ(y_t / (l_{t-1} + b_{t-1})) + (1-γ)s_{t-m}`. #
/// Errors Returns a lowercase message when the seasonal period is zero, the
/// series covers fewer than two seasons, a value is not finite or not strictly
/// positive, a smoothing parameter leaves `[0, 1]`, or a level or seasonal
/// index is zero where the recursion divides by it.
inline Term holt_winters_mul(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                             const Term &a3, const Term &a4) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4};
  return apply("holt_winters_mul", args, 5);
}

/// `hooi(t, ranks, sweeps, tol)`: Tucker approximation of tensor `t` by
/// higher-order orthogonal iteration, returning `list(core, factors, error)`.
/// Refine a truncated HOSVD using higher-order orthogonal iteration. Each
/// coordinate step computes the leading singular subspace after projecting all
/// other modes. Ranks are upper bounds and may be clamped to the available
/// subspace. Initialization is deterministic HOSVD; HOOI can converge to a
/// local optimum or stationary point. Inspect `relative_error` independently
/// from `converged`. Exhausting the sweep budget returns the best observed
/// approximation with `converged = false`. Residuals near floating-point
/// roundoff also terminate the iteration. Input normalization protects
/// intermediate norm calculations at uniformly small/large scales. No Gram
/// matrices or condition-number squaring are used. Zero tensors use a rank-one
/// zero core. # Errors Non-finite data, empty modes, invalid
/// ranks/tolerance/budget, SVD failure, or arithmetic overflow return an error.
inline Term hooi(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                 const Term &a3) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3};
  return apply("hooi", args, 4);
}

/// `hook_lengths(shape)`: Young diagram hook lengths for integer partition
/// `shape`.
inline Term hook_lengths(const Term &a0) {
  Term args[] = {a0};
  return apply("hook_lengths", args, 1);
}

/// `hosvd(t, ranks)`: truncated higher-order SVD of tensor `t` returning
/// `list(core, factors, singular_values)`. The higher-order SVD (Tucker
/// decomposition) of a dense tensor. For each mode the tensor is unfolded to
/// `n_k x prod(rest)`, the leading left singular vectors of the unfolding
/// become the factor, and the core is the tensor contracted with every factor.
/// `ranks` may be `None` for the numerical multilinear rank of the unfoldings
/// (at most `min(n_k, prod(rest))`, and less when an unfolding is rank
/// deficient in floating point); a requested rank above that is clamped to it.
/// The decomposition is exact before truncation and gives `||T - C x U||_F <=
/// sqrt(sum_k sum_{j > r_k} sigma_{k,j}^2)`. # Errors Fails when `ranks` does
/// not have one entry per mode, when a requested rank is zero, when a mode is
/// empty, or when a mode unfolding has no nonzero singular value.
inline Term hosvd(const Term &a0, const Term &a1) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1};
  return apply("hosvd", args, 2);
}

