/// product-limit estimate of the survival function. `time` holds the observed
/// times and `event` is true when the observation ended in the event of
/// interest and false when it was censored. The inputs are not modified; the
/// estimate is computed on an internal sorted copy. `conf` is the two-sided
/// confidence level and must lie strictly between 0 and 1. # Errors Returns an
/// error for empty or mismatched inputs, non-finite times, a confidence level
/// outside `(0, 1)`, or a sample in which every observation is censored.
inline Term kaplan_meier(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2};
  return apply("kaplan_meier", args, 3);
}

