/// `lerch(z, s, a)`: Lerch transcendent `Phi(z, s, a) = sum_{n=0}^infty z^n /
/// (n + a)^s`. The Lerch transcendent `Φ(z, s, a) = Σ_{k=0}^∞ z^k / (k+a)^s`
/// for real `s`, real `a > 0` and `z < 1` (the standard range). For `|z| <=
/// 9/10` the defining series is summed directly. For `s > 0` and `|z| > 9/10`
/// the Euler integral `Φ = 1/Γ(s) ∫_0^∞ t^(s-1) e^(-a t)/(1 - z e^(-t)) dt` is
/// evaluated by double-exponential quadrature, which covers `z < 0` (`|z| > 1`
/// included) as well as `z ↑ 1`. Non-positive integer `s` use the rational form
/// `(z d/dz + a)^n 1/(1-z)`. Non-integer orders in `[-15.5, 0)` use an Euler
/// integral with the order shifted above zero. At `z = 1` the analytic
/// continuation `ζ(s, a)` is returned. Outside the implemented range the result
/// is `NaN`.
