/// Native Genz-Malik cubature: physical same-unit coordinates, independently
/// measured output, explicit evaluation limit and volume-dimensioned absolute
/// tolerance. Adaptive Genz-Malik cubature over the box `[lo, hi]`. Each region
/// is integrated with the degree-7 Genz-Malik rule (`1 + 4n + 2n(n-1) + 2^n`
/// points) whose embedded degree-5 rule gives the error estimate; the region
/// with the largest error is bisected along the axis with the largest fourth
/// divided difference. The box is first split uniformly into a few sub-boxes so
/// that narrow peaks are not missed. Stops when the total error is below
/// `max(abs_tol, rel_tol * |value|)` or after `max_evals` integrand evaluations
/// (`converged == false`). Intended for 2 to about 8 dimensions. A bisection
/// only replaces a region by its two halves, so the regions always tile the box
/// exactly: their volumes sum to the box volume and no two overlap. `value` and
/// `error` are the sums of the region values and of the region estimates; the
/// estimate is the embedded degree-5/7 difference, a heuristic rather than a
/// rigorous bound (see the module limitations).
inline Term
num_analysis_cubature_genz_malik_compiled(const Term &a0, const Term &a1,
                                          const Term &a2, const Term &a3,
                                          const Term &a4, const Term &a5) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5};
  return apply("num_analysis_cubature_genz_malik_compiled", args, 6);
}

