/// Native2D Filon cosine/sine quadrature: phase coefficients have one dimension
/// P,omega has1/(P*coordinate),amplitude references preserve arbitrary ordinate
/// units. Two-dimensional Filon quadrature of an oscillatory integrand over a
/// box. The integrand is `f(x, y) * cos(omega * phi(x, y))` (`cosine = true`)
/// or `f(x, y) * sin(omega * phi(x, y))` (`cosine = false`), for the linear
/// phase `phi(x, y) = a x + b y` with `phase = [a, b]`. The amplitude is
/// interpolated by a tensor product of quadratic Lagrange polynomials, one per
/// double panel and axis, and each oscillatory moment is integrated exactly (it
/// is the 1-D [`filon`] functional), so the accuracy does not degrade as
/// `|omega|` grows. The panel count is doubled from one until the difference
/// between successive sweeps is at most `tol * max(|value|, 1)`, so `omega = 0`
/// reproduces the classical Simpson rule (exact for a quadratic amplitude).
/// Invalid input (a box dimension list other than two, `hi <= lo`, a non-finite
