/// Native Gaussian importance sampling using measured target/proposal models;
/// integrand references match their coordinate domain. Output has ordinate
/// units, not ordinate times length; ESS remains dimensionless.
/// Importance-sampling estimate of `∫ f(x) p_target(x) dx`. Draws `n` points
/// from `proposal` and averages `f(x) * p_target(x) / p_proposal(x)`. Because
/// the weight has mean one under the proposal, the estimator is unbiased for
/// the target integral whatever the shift; what the shift costs is variance,
/// visible in the effective sample size. The proposal must be non-degenerate
/// and have at least the support of the target, otherwise the weights are not
/// finite and the estimate is not defined. The error is the sample standard
/// error of the weighted terms, and the effective sample size is `(Σ w)^2 / Σ
/// w^2`.
