/// Normalized native rootfind::newton_bracketed: parameters Float vector
/// length3, exact nonnegative integer controls length1, positive coordinate
/// reference D,positive value reference E,evaluation budget,then2 normalized
/// Float callbacks. Results restore D*E for integrals,D for roots,E for sums.
/// Error=None means native method supplies no finite error estimate;
/// convergence flag retains native stopping status where available. Safeguarded
/// Newton on a sign-changing bracket `[a, b]`. Newton steps must lie in the
/// central half of the current bracket; otherwise bisection guarantees
/// progress. Convergence uses bracket width, not the Newton step size, which
/// can be tiny far from a root. `tol` is a relative/absolute width tolerance
/// scaled by `1 + |x|`. # Errors [`RootError::NotBracketed`] /
/// [`RootError::NoConvergence`]. [`RootError::Invalid`] for non-finite inputs,
/// function or derivative values, or a non-positive tolerance.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args>
inline Value num_analysis_newton_bracketed_scaled(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_analysis_newton_bracketed_scaled",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

/// Genuine matrix-free trust-region Newton-CG: physical point,positive
/// coordinate/objective references,explicit normalized-coordinate metric
/// options,shared callback evaluation limit,then normalized
/// objective/gradient/Hessian-vector callbacks. Exact derivative actions come
/// from the supplied callbacks; no finite-difference substitution. Returns
/// physical x,value,gradient norm plus actual native status and work counters.
/// Minimize a smooth objective using only vector actions. `gradient(x, out)`
/// and `hessian_vector(x, direction, out)` must fill every output element.
/// Buffers are reset to NaN before each callback, so missing writes are
/// detected. Non-finite trial objectives/gradients are rejected; the last
/// accepted point is retained. No parallel callback calls occur. # Errors
/// Returns an error for invalid options/input, a non-finite initial value or
/// gradient, or a non-finite Hessian action/CG intermediate.
