/// Adaptive BDF with dense output and event detection. Set controls[1] to 1 to
/// use the Jacobian of the retained RHS tape. An omitted or other value uses
/// finite differences, evaluated concurrently for systems with at least 64
/// state components. The positive maximum order controls[0] defaults to one and
/// is capped at five. Config rtol and atol apply to the normalized state.
/// Config h0, hmin and hmax are physical step magnitudes, and zero h0 selects
/// the initial step automatically. The required config max_steps bounds
/// attempts, including rejected steps. Each event supplies program, terminal
/// and direction (-1, 0 or 1). The maxeval argument bounds tape evaluations.
/// [`bdf_with`] with concurrently evaluated finite-difference Jacobians. The
/// right-hand side must be `Sync`; the solution is bit-identical. It pays from
/// `n` of a few hundred when one evaluation of `f` is expensive (measured 1.35
/// at `n = 100` to 1.56 at `n = 400`); below `STIFF_PAR_MIN_N` it uses the
/// serial Jacobian. The Radau solver gains nothing (Newton / LU dominate: 1.08,
/// 0.99, 0.92), so there is no `radau_with_par`. # Errors As [`bdf_with`].
