/// Native ode::solve_fixed_events; independently measured initial components
/// and physical times are normalized by the retained RHS tape references.
/// Config rtol/atol are explicit normalized-state tolerances; h0/hmin/hmax are
/// physical times and max_steps is mandatory. Controls contain
/// steps/order/stages as documented by the native function; events contain
/// program/terminal/direction. Real native evaluation and retained sample
/// budgets are enforced. Integrates in `steps` equal steps and locates events.
/// # How an event is located without a dense output A fixed-step method has no
/// interpolant, so there is nothing to Brent-iterate on. It is a *one-step*
/// method, however, which means the state at any intermediate time is just
/// another application of the same step from the same start: the locator
/// bisects the step length, re-integrating the partial step each time, until
/// the bracket is below `1e-13`. That is exact for the method — the located
/// state is a point of the method's own trajectory, not of an interpolant — and
/// it costs about fifty evaluations per event, which is the right trade for a
/// method that is cheap by construction. A `terminal` event stops the
/// integration; the trajectory then ends at the event point. # Errors As
/// [`solve_fixed`].
