/// receives(time,position) and outputs position/time²; velocity references are
/// derived from position/time. All8native methods and original native dense
/// data are preserved. Integrates a second-order separable system `q' = p`, `p'
/// = accel(t, q)` using a symplectic or geometric integrator over `span = (t0,
/// t1)` with `steps` steps. For autonomous acceleration `accel(q)` with
/// splitting methods (`StormerVerlet`, `Ruth4`, `Yoshida6`, `Yoshida8`), this
/// uses the exact velocity-Verlet composition matching
/// `rssn::kernels::ode_ext::symplectic_split` (`Rssn_Numeric::ode_symplectic`),
/// extended to support time-dependent forces, `Ruth3`, and implicit
/// Gauss–Legendre methods (`ImplicitMidpoint`, `GaussLegendre4`,
/// `GaussLegendre6`). # Errors [`OdeGeomError::Domain`] for non-finite inputs
