/// Native ode_stiff::radau5_jac; independently measured initial components and
/// physical times are normalized by the retained RHS tape references. Config
/// rtol/atol are explicit normalized-state tolerances; h0/hmin/hmax are
/// physical times and max_steps is mandatory. Controls contain
/// steps/order/stages as documented by the native function; events contain
/// program/terminal/direction. Real native evaluation and retained sample
/// budgets are enforced. Radau IIA(5) integration with a user-supplied Jacobian
/// `jac(t, y)`. The method is L-stable, stiffly accurate and of order 5. The
/// stage system is solved by simplified Newton iteration with a single LU
/// factorisation reused across iterations and across steps whose step size is
/// (nearly) unchanged; the Jacobian is refreshed only when the Newton iteration
/// fails to converge. The error estimate is the embedded third-order formula of
