/// physical times and max_steps is mandatory. Controls contain
/// steps/order/stages as documented by the native function; events contain
/// program/terminal/direction. Real native evaluation and retained sample
/// budgets are enforced. Adaptive SDIRK3(2) with event detection on its cubic
/// Hermite dense output. Events follow the conventions of the other
/// integrators: a sign change of `g(t, y)` is located by Brent iteration on the
/// continuous extension, `direction` selects rising, falling or both crossings,
/// and a `terminal` event ends the run at the event point, which is recorded as
/// the last sample of [`OdeSolution::t`]. Non-terminal events are recorded in
/// [`OdeSolution::events`] and integration continues to `t1`. The located event
/// time inherits the `O(h³)` accuracy of the interpolation (see the module
/// limitations), not the `1e-14` bracket tolerance of the root finder. # Errors
