/// output V for initial data or V/L^2 for Poisson; secondary V/T only for wave.
/// Method SparseLu/Cg/MeanFree for elliptic,Upwind/LaxWendroff for advection;
/// relative>0. Dedicated Laplace ignores primary; other unused
/// coefficients/secondary are explicit placeholder Values. Solves `u_t = alpha
/// u_xx` on `grid` with Crank-Nicolson time stepping (`steps` equal steps up to
/// `t_end`); `bc = [left, right]`. The scheme is second-order in space and time
/// and unconditionally stable. # Errors [`PdeError::InvalidInput`] for a bad
/// grid, step count or `alpha <= 0`; [`PdeError::SolveFailed`] or
/// [`PdeError::NonFinite`] otherwise.
