num_analysis_sde_adaptive_noncommutative_with(const Term &a0, const Term &a1,
                                              const Term &a2, const Term &a3,
                                              const Term &a4, const Term &a5) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5};
  return apply("num_analysis_sde_adaptive_noncommutative_with", args, 6);
}

/// Actual native sde_adaptive_stratonovich_with with independently scaled
/// physical state, normalized rtol/atol, seed, max_steps, and explicit
/// evaluation budget. Noncommutative variants require bounded cells/terms and
/// retain genuine conditional Levy areas. Adaptive-step integration of a
/// **Stratonovich** SDE `dX = a dt + g o dW` with commutative noise on `[t0,
/// t1]`, by exact conversion to Ito form. The drift is replaced by the
/// Ito-equivalent drift ([`stratonovich_to_ito_drift`]) and
/// [`sde_adaptive_with`] runs on the Ito SDE `dX = a~ dt + g dW`, which has the
/// same solution process. The returned path is therefore the *controlled
/// Ito-Milstein solution of the equivalent Ito SDE*; it converges to the
/// Stratonovich solution of the original coefficients (for `dX = sigma X o dW`
/// to `X_0 exp(sigma W_T)`), with the error control of [`sde_adaptive_with`]
/// applied to the converted drift. The conversion uses finite-difference
/// derivatives of `g`, which costs `2m + 1` extra diffusion evaluations per
/// drift evaluation. # Errors As [`sde_adaptive_with`].
