num_analysis_sde_adaptive_stratonovich_with(const Term &a0, const Term &a1,
                                            const Term &a2, const Term &a3,
                                            const Term &a4, const Term &a5) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5};
  return apply("num_analysis_sde_adaptive_stratonovich_with", args, 6);
}

/// Actual native sde_adaptive_with with independently scaled physical state,
/// normalized rtol/atol, seed, max_steps, and explicit evaluation budget.
/// Noncommutative variants require bounded cells/terms and retain genuine
/// conditional Levy areas. Adaptive-step integration of an Ito SDE with
/// commutative noise on `[t0, t1]`. Each step computes the Euler-Maruyama and
/// the Milstein update from the same Brownian increment; the Milstein
/// correction plus the trapezoidal drift correction `h |a(y_EM) - a(y)| / 2`
/// estimate the local error of the former (so additive noise and strongly
/// varying drifts both control the step). A step is accepted when the scaled
/// error `max_i |delta_i| / (atol + rtol |y_i|)` is at most one (the tolerance
/// bounds the local, not the global, pathwise error; the global error
/// accumulates like a random walk). Rejected increments are split by Brownian
/// bridges and re-used, so the realised path is a genuine Brownian sample
/// independent of the step sequence. The returned solution is the Milstein one.
