/// Actual native conditional Levy areas. Supplied increments have sqrt(time)
/// units and output flattened m by m Ito integrals have time units. Samples the
/// iterated Ito integrals `I_jl` of one step of length `h`. The integrals are
/// drawn conditionally on the increments `dw` by the Fourier expansion of the
/// Brownian bridge (Kloeden, Platen and Wright) with the Gaussian approximation
/// of the truncated tail that reproduces its full conditional covariance
/// (Wiktorsson's improvement): with `xi = dw / sqrt(h)`, `I_jl / h = xi_j xi_l
/// / 2 + A_jl + sqrt(rho) (mu_j xi_l - mu_l xi_j) + sqrt(rho) nu_jl` for `j <
/// l`, where `A` is the Fourier sum over `terms` modes, `rho` the tail sum
/// divided by `2 pi^2`, and `mu`, `nu` standard normal. The remainder error
/// decays like `1 / terms^{3/2}` in distribution; a few terms suffice for
/// strong order one. `dw` contains the `m` supplied increments. The returned
/// matrix is flat and row-major. Pair evaluation can run in parallel, with the
/// same RNG draws and floating-point summation order for every worker count.
