/// Actual native MLMC with coupled fine/coarse Brownian paths. Payoff compiled
/// program receives physical state components; target RMSE and
/// estimate/standard-error have payoff units and variance has their square.
/// Explicit hierarchy/sample/work caps bound all native levels. Estimate a
/// terminal SDE expectation with multilevel Monte Carlo. Estimates the expected
/// value `E[payoff(X_{t1})]` of a terminal functional of an SDE `dX = a(t, X)
/// dt + G(t, X) dW` using Giles' Multilevel Monte Carlo (MLMC) method with
/// coupled fine/coarse Brownian paths (`\\Delta W^{(c)}_k = \\Delta
/// W^{(f)}_{2k} + \\Delta W^{(f)}_{2k+1}`) and optimal sample allocation `N_l
/// \\propto \\sqrt{V_l / C_l}`. Each (level, sample index) draws from its own
/// deterministic seeded stream. A coupled fine/coarse pair shares that stream.
/// The estimates for a given seed may differ from versions that reused streams
/// across levels. # Errors Returns [`SdeError`] if options or callback
/// dimensions are invalid or if any simulated trajectory becomes non-finite.
/// Returns [`SdeError::StepLimit`] if cancelled at a checkpoint between solves
/// and payoff evaluations.
