/// physical negative potential. Binding has energy units and may be negative
/// when initial T+B>0; fictitious step has energy*time units; the returned
/// error is explicitly in the native normalized state metric. Time-transformed
/// leapfrog for `H = T(p) + V(q)` with `V < 0`. Uses the extended Hamiltonian
/// `K = ln(T + B) - ln(-V)` with `B = -E0` (`E0` the energy to preserve); the
/// fictitious step `h` corresponds to the physical step `h / (T + B)`, which is
/// `h r / (GM)` for Kepler (a Sundman transformation `dt = r ds`). The scheme
