/// argument tolerance, positive iteration budget, callback. The root and
/// tolerance have callback-domain dimensions; residual dimensions are
/// independent. Returns root/evaluations without an extra residual evaluation.
/// Endpoint samples count as evaluations, callback failures propagate
/// unchanged, and iteration exhaustion is an explicit error. Brent's method on
/// a bracketing interval `[a, b]`. # Errors [`RootError::NotBracketed`] if the
/// endpoints have the same nonzero sign, [`RootError::Invalid`] for non-finite
/// inputs, non-positive tolerance, or non-finite callback values, and
/// [`RootError::NoConvergence`] at the limit.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
