/// Dimensionless nonlinear system solver: initial vector,positive
/// tolerance,max_iterations,max_evaluations,residual callback. Callback input
/// and output retain the initial vector length. Returns x,evaluations; callback
/// failures and iteration exhaustion are explicit errors. Broyden's "good"
/// method: finite-difference Jacobian at the start, then rank-one updates of
/// its inverse-applied form (Sherman-Morrison on `B`). # Errors As
/// [`newton_system`].
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_broyden(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_broyden", std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

/// Measured nonlinear problem with explicit coordinate_scale and value_scale,
/// dimensionless tolerance, max_iterations and max_evaluations controls. Solves
/// in normalized coordinates/residuals. Arguments: initial, controls, optional
/// lower/upper, objective/residual, optional gradient. Gradient units are
/// objective/coordinate. Homogeneous coordinate and residual vectors; callback
/// failures propagate and budgets are shared. Broyden's "good" method:
/// finite-difference Jacobian at the start, then rank-one updates of its
/// inverse-applied form (Sherman-Morrison on `B`). # Errors As
/// [`newton_system`].
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_broyden_scaled(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_broyden_scaled",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

