/// Krawczyk existence and uniqueness test. The callback must enclose the
/// function and derivative on each entire normalized disk. None means the test
/// could not certify a root. Certifies existence and uniqueness of a simple
/// complex root of `f` inside `ball`. Uses the 1D complex Krawczyk operator:
/// `K(B) = m - f(m)/f'(m) + (1 - f'(B)/f'(m)) * (B - m)`. Returns `Some(K(B))`
/// if `K(B)` lies strictly inside `ball`.
