/// Krawczyk existence and uniqueness test for a normalized complex box. The
/// Jacobian callback must enclose every derivative on the entire box. None
/// means no certificate was obtained. Multi-dimensional complex Krawczyk root
/// certification for `F(z) = 0`. Given a box `balls` (`[B_0, ..., B_{n-1}]`),
/// midpoint evaluation `f_mid = F(m)`, and Jacobian enclosure `jac_box =
/// J_F(B)` (evaluated over `balls`), computes `K(B) = m - R * f_mid + (I - R *
/// J_F(B)) * (B - m)` where `R ~ J_F(m)^{-1}`. Returns `Some(K(B))` if every
/// component `K(B)_i` lies strictly inside `B_i`.
