/// Returns a truncated measured Koenigs coordinate estimate with its
/// fixed-point closure error and actual counts. The supplied multiplier must
/// have magnitude strictly between zero and one. Uses positive coordinate scale
/// and closure tolerance, and bounded iterations and callbacks. Computes the
/// Koenigs coordinate of an attracting fixed point. Computes Koenigs's
/// linearizing coordinate $\\psi(z) = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\lambda^{-n}
/// (f^{\\circ n}(z) - `z_0`)$ near an attracting fixed point $`z_0`$ ($0 <
/// |\\lambda| < 1$), satisfying $\\psi(f(z)) = \\lambda \\psi(z)$. # Errors
/// Returns an error if the multiplier does not satisfy `0 < |lambda| < 1`.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args>
inline Value num_complex_dynamics_koenigs_checked(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_complex_dynamics_koenigs_checked",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

