/// Returns sampled logarithmic-derivative moments of (z-center)/radius, the
/// largest coarse/fine difference, and sample/evaluation counts. Takes a
/// measured center, radius, callback value scale, initial sample count, maximum
/// moment, host budget, analytic function and derivative. Computes power-sum
/// moments $`s_k` = \\frac{1}{2\\pi i} \\oint_{|z-c|=r} z^k \\frac{f'(z)}{f(z)}
/// dz$ for $k = 0, \\dots, \\text{max\\_moment}$ using the periodic trapezoidal
/// rule. # Errors Returns an error for an invalid radius or sample count, or if
/// the function is nearly zero on the circle.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
