/// Simulate a measured continuous state-space model on a strictly increasing
/// time grid. Hold each input row until the next time and return one measured
/// output row per grid point. Simulates a continuous-time model on the strictly
/// increasing time grid `t` from initial state `x0` under piecewise-constant
/// (zero-order-hold) inputs `u`, where `u[k]` is held across `[t[k], t[k +
/// 1])`. Each step uses exact zero-order-hold discretisation via
/// [`StateSpace::c2d_zoh`], caching `(Ad, Bd)` whenever consecutive step sizes
/// match to a relative tolerance of `1e-12`. Uniform grids compute the matrix
