/// Dimension-aware serial quadrature with a strict callback evaluation budget.
/// Fixed rules: a,b,order,max_evaluations,callback. Romberg/tanh-sinh:
/// a,b,tolerance,max_levels,max_evaluations,callback. Semi-infinite rules:
/// finite_bound,tolerance,max_evaluations,callback; left-infinite integrates
/// (-infinity,bound], right-infinite [bound,infinity). Full infinite rule:
/// tolerance,max_evaluations,callback. Adaptive results include
/// value,error,evaluations,converged; fixed rules report value,evaluations.
/// Callback failures propagate unchanged. `n`-point Gauss-Legendre quadrature
/// of `f` on `[a, b]`.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_gauss_legendre(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_gauss_legendre",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

