/// Native staggered acoustic call in a mechanical reference frame. In dimension
/// d, density is Mass/Length^d and pressure is Energy/Length^d, representing
/// the explicitly reduced continuum. Velocity is Length/Time and total energy
/// is Energy. All numeric coordinates, spacings, speed, density and arrays are
/// normalized by these references. Compiled physical callbacks retain
/// dimensions and finite evaluation budgets; failed mutations invalidate their
/// solver handle. Sets a spatially varying medium from `x ↦ (c, ρ)` sampled at
/// the cell centres, and re-derives [`Acoustics::dt`] and the PML from the
/// result. The density on a face is the harmonic mean of the two cells it
/// separates and the bulk modulus of a cell is `ρc²`, which is what keeps the
/// scheme second order across an interface (an interface is exact when it lies
/// on a face). Call this before stepping: the fields, the clock and the sources
/// are left alone. # Errors A non-positive or non-finite `c` or `ρ` at a cell
/// centre.
