/// Solves the interior or exterior Laplace problem with linear elements. Each
/// vertex has one Potential or Flux coefficient in the supplied frame's field
/// or field-per-length reference. Use the boundary-field accessor for the
/// resulting vertex coefficients. Solves the interior Laplace problem with
/// **continuous piecewise-linear** potential and flux on the triangulated
/// surface, by collocation at the vertices (dense LU). `bcs` gives the data per
/// **vertex**: the potential or the derivative along the outward normal.
/// Single-layer integrals use adaptive subdivision away from the collocation
/// point and a Duffy transformation for the elements that contain it; the
/// double-layer kernel vanishes on those (planar) elements, and the
/// free-term/diagonal is fixed by the rigid-body identity `Σ_j H_ij = 0`.
/// Exterior problems: pass `exterior = true` (orientation reversed and the flux
/// sign convention of [`solve_laplace_bem_3d_exterior`]). # Errors For an
/// invalid mesh, wrong data length, or a singular system (pure Neumann interior
/// problems are singular).
inline Term num_grid_bem_p1(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                            const Term &a3) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3};
  return apply("num_grid_bem_p1", args, 4);
}

/// Solves the interior or exterior Laplace problem with ACA-compressed linear
/// elements and GMRES. Each vertex has one Potential or Flux coefficient in the
/// supplied frame's field or field-per-length reference. The positive
/// tolerance, at most one, controls both ACA and GMRES. Solves the Laplace
/// problem with **linear (P1) elements** like [`solve_laplace_bem_3d_p1`], but
/// with hierarchical-matrix compression. The vertex collocation matrices `G`
/// and `H` are assembled lazily from the element integrals (adaptive
/// subdivision away from the collocation point, Duffy transformation on
/// elements containing it), far blocks of the vertex cluster tree are
/// compressed by adaptive cross approximation, the rigid-body diagonal of `H`
/// follows from one compressed matrix-vector product with the vector of ones,
/// and the system is solved by Jacobi-preconditioned GMRES. # Errors For an
/// invalid mesh, wrong data length, non-finite data, a pure Neumann interior
/// problem (singular) or GMRES failure.
inline Term num_grid_bem_p1_aca(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                                const Term &a3, const Term &a4, const Term &a5,
                                const Term &a6, const Term &a7,
                                const Term &a8) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8};
  return apply("num_grid_bem_p1_aca", args, 9);
}

