/// Prepares an interior three-dimensional Laplace boundary-element solve and
/// stores the constant-panel collocation operator and LU factors. Supply
/// Potential or Flux for each triangle in mesh order. The plan retains the
/// mesh's reference frame. Dense storage is quadratic in the panel count.
/// Factors the system for the supplied trianglewise boundary kinds. # Errors
/// Rejects invalid meshes, a mismatched number of kinds, singular systems and
/// non-finite boundary operators. Reports cancellation.
inline Term num_grid_bem_prepare3(const Term &a0, const Term &a1) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1};
  return apply("num_grid_bem_prepare3", args, 2);
}

/// Native BEM call. Numeric coordinates are normalized by the supplied PDE
/// frame length, potentials by its field reference, and fluxes by field/length.
/// Outputs retain explicit physical reference witnesses. Self-check of the 3D
/// BEM: solves the Dirichlet problem `u = x` on a 320-triangle unit icosphere
/// with [`solve_laplace_bem_3d_mesh`] and verifies the recovered flux against
/// the exact `q = n_x`. This is the former argument-less entry point; the
/// general solver is [`solve_laplace_bem_3d_mesh`]. # Errors Returns an error
/// if the solve fails or the flux error exceeds 5 %.
inline Term num_grid_bem_selfcheck3() {
  return apply("num_grid_bem_selfcheck3", nullptr, 0);
}

