/// Advances a 2D heat field with Crank–Nicolson ADI. The x-fastest initial
/// field provides all four fixed Dirichlet edges, which retain their values
/// throughout the solve. Supply spacing in units of length_reference,
/// diffusivity in length_reference^2/time_reference, the time step in
/// time_reference, and temperature in value_reference. The returned field keeps
/// its grid references. Evolves a two-dimensional heat field with fixed
/// Dirichlet boundaries. The x-fastest initial field supplies the four boundary
/// edges. They remain fixed during both ADI half-steps. The grid has `nx * ny`
/// nodes, including the boundaries. Spacings must be positive, and diffusivity
/// and the time step must be nonnegative. A grid without interior nodes is
/// stationary. # Errors Returns an error for shape mismatches, non-finite data
/// or results, invalid physical parameters, unrepresentable coefficients, or
/// cancellation.
inline Term num_grid_cnm_solve_heat_equation_2d_cn_adi_fixed_boundary(
    const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2, const Term &a3,
    const Term &a4, const Term &a5, const Term &a6) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6};
  return apply("num_grid_cnm_solve_heat_equation_2d_cn_adi_fixed_boundary",
               args, 7);
}

