/// Native ETDRK4 with a genuinely coupled compiled nonlinear map: two scalar
/// programs per complex mode (real then imaginary), each taking coherent
/// [time,re0,im0,...]. At most31 modes fit the compiled ABI's63 inputs. Linear
/// symbols are normalized inverse-time coefficients; nonlinear outputs must
/// have field/time units. Native x-fastest spectral extent ordering and exact
/// ETDRK4 stepping are preserved. Fourth-order ETDRK4 time stepping of `u_t = L
/// u + N(u, t)` in the spectral domain. Integrates `u_t = L u + N(u, t)` in the
/// spectral domain with the fourth-order exponential time differencing
/// Runge–Kutta scheme of Cox and Matthews (contour-integral coefficients of
/// Kassam and Trefethen). `lin[p]` is the (diagonal) linear symbol;
/// `nonlinear(t, uh)` returns the spectral transform of `N`.
inline Term num_grid_etdrk4(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                            const Term &a3, const Term &a4, const Term &a5) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5};
  return apply("num_grid_etdrk4", args, 6);
}

