/// Actual native spatial Dörfler refinement, independently from temporal
/// adaptivity. Positive Length/Time/field references determine
/// coefficient/source units and residual-indicator reference. A conservative
/// worst-case refinement/DOF bound is checked before native allocation; actual
/// returned space, field and estimator history are retained. Adaptive solution
/// of the static problem: solve, estimate, mark and refine. Starting from
/// `mesh`, the loop solves `-∇·(k ∇u) + c u = f(t, x)` with [`solve_static`],
/// estimates the error with [`error_indicators`], marks the smallest set of
/// cells whose indicators carry the fraction `theta` of `Σ η_T²` (Dörfler
/// marking), refines them with [`SimplexMesh::refine_marked`] and repeats. It
/// stops when the total estimate is at most `tolerance` or after `max_steps`
/// refinements (so at most `max_steps + 1` solves). `degree` selects P1 or P2.
/// # Errors If `degree` is not 1 or 2, `theta` is outside `(0, 1]`, `max_steps`
/// is zero, or one of the solves fails.
