/// Native elasticity call in an explicit mechanical reference frame. Numeric
/// displacements/coordinates use Length, body forces use Mass/(Length^2
/// Time^2), stress/Young modulus use Mass/(Length Time^2), and density uses
/// Mass/Length^3. Reduced 2D hyperelastic energies are per unit out-of-plane
/// thickness. Outputs retain distinct dimensional reference witnesses. Native
/// DOF, nonlinear work, callbacks and allocation budgets are checked.
/// Integrates `M a + f_int(u) = f_ext(t)` from the given initial state with
/// fixed step `dt`. The external load is the body force and the nominal
/// tractions of `prob` (constant in time, applied suddenly at `t = 0`);
/// displacement conditions are evaluated at the new time. `observer` is called
/// after every step with the new state. # Errors If an element inverts, Newton
/// fails or the effective matrix is singular.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_grid_hyper_dynamic(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_grid_hyper_dynamic",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

