/// (u²/2)_{x_a} = 0` on a 1D, 2D or 3D grid. The cells are stored flat, with x
/// fastest. Uses the multi-dimensional Lax–Friedrichs flux with equal
/// numerical-viscosity shares per axis and zero-gradient outflow boundaries.
/// The one-dimensional stencil agrees with [`solve_burgers_1d`] up to
/// arithmetic roundoff. See [`solve_burgers_nd_with_boundaries`] for the
/// stability condition. # Errors As [`solve_burgers_nd_with_boundaries`].
