/// reference. Spacing, velocity, diffusivity and time are normalized in the
/// supplied frame. Zero steps or a zero time step preserves the coefficients.
/// Advances an existing complex Fourier spectrum by the configured Euler steps.
/// The spectrum uses the unnormalized forward transform of [`fft3d`] and the
/// same axis order, with x varying fastest, then y, then z. [`ifft3d`] divides
/// by the grid size on returning to physical space. A zero-step or
/// zero-time-step call keeps all validated coefficients unchanged. # Errors
