/// Native exact algebraic topology with session-owned, kind/version checked
/// complex, chain and presentation handles. Complex inputs/exports use CSR
/// offsets/indices. Handles are invalid in other sessions and after release;
/// all objects own their data. Finite construction bounds: 4096 simplices, 12
/// vertices per simplex, 65536 face/storage words, 256 generators per chain
/// group and 128 x 128 exact matrix elimination. Presentation simplification
/// accepts sixteen generators and 256 input word coefficients with the native
/// 4000-word intermediate limit; product frontiers are bounded to 1048576
/// coefficient slots. Cubical chains accept 64 pixels; direct cubical Betti
/// accepts 4096. Filtrations carry a canonical value_unit witness verified
/// against stored radius dimensions. Bars use explicit essential flags and zero
/// death placeholders; bottleneck inputs are births/deaths/essential records
/// and unequal essential counts give positive infinity. Products return None on
/// their native simplex limit; malformed inputs and adapter budget exhaustion
/// are errors. Pure source algorithms are invoked in RSSN kernels; opaque
/// payloads contain only session handles, never serialized pointers. The
/// abelianisation of a presented group: `Z^rank + torsion`.
inline Term num_homology_abelianization(const Term &a0) {
  Term args[] = {a0};
  return apply("num_homology_abelianization", args, 1);
}

/// Native exact algebraic topology with session-owned, kind/version checked
