/// Damped nonlinear least squares with a scoped vector residual callback.
/// Initial parameters and residuals may have independent dimensions. Returns
/// the best point, residual norm, work counters, convergence and explicit
/// stopping status; callback failures propagate. Minimise one half of the
/// squared residual norm using a damped, column-scaled augmented SVD. The
/// Jacobian may be analytic or safely differenced. The reported scaled gradient
/// is formed from `J[:,j]/max(abs(J[:,j]))` and `f/max(abs(f))`; it is a
/// dimensionless first-order test, not a root proof. Trial steps are accepted
/// only on positive actual and predicted decrease. Residual length must remain
/// constant on every evaluation. # Errors Invalid input, malformed callback
/// results, or a failed decomposition return a [`LeastSquaresError`].
/// Nonconvergence is reported as a result status.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_least_squares(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_least_squares",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

