/// Native tensor decomposition with explicit reference scale and bounded
/// factor/order/sweep storage. Factors are normalized; reconstructed tensors
/// retain the input physical domain. CP (CANDECOMP/PARAFAC) decomposition by
/// alternating least squares. Factorises a dense tensor as `T ~= sum_r lambda_r
/// a_r o b_r o c_r` for `options.rank` components, by solving one matricised
/// least-squares problem per mode per sweep (the standard ALS update on the
/// mode-`k` unfolding against the Khatri-Rao product of the other factors).
/// Factors are initialised uniformly at random from `options.seed` and
/// normalised after every update, with the removed norms kept in
/// [`CpDecomposition::weights`]. A rank-`R` tensor whose factors span a
/// full-rank problem is recovered to rounding error, but the factors themselves
/// are only determined up to permutation and scaling: compare reconstructions,
/// not factors. CP is ill-posed, so the result says what happened rather than
/// assuming success. `converged` means the residual reached `tol`; `stagnated`
/// means sweeps stopped improving while the residual stayed above `tol`;
/// `diverged` means a weight blew up, which is how a degenerate problem (border
/// rank below rank) shows itself; `rank_deficient` means the least-squares
/// system was numerically rank deficient in its direct SVD solve. # Errors
/// Returns an error for a tensor of rank below 2, an empty dimension,
/// non-finite entries/options, a zero rank, zero sweeps, or rescaling overflow.
/// Updates solve the Khatri-Rao least-squares system directly by SVD, once per
/// mode, avoiding normal equations and squared condition numbers. Input
/// normalization protects uniformly very small or very large tensors.
inline Term num_linear_cp_als(const Term &a0, const Term &a1) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1};
  return apply("num_linear_cp_als", args, 2);
}

