/// Native exact sparse/domain operation specialized to BigRational or a
/// validated prime field. Coefficients are normalized dimensionless exact
/// values; finite shape, coefficient-bit and work budgets are enforced. The
/// minimal polynomial of a square matrix over `GF(p)` by Wiedemann's algorithm,
/// monic, lowest degree first. The algorithm flattens `matrix` once into a
/// Montgomery-domain CSR workspace, multiplies by the matrix `2n` times per
/// trial with delayed `u128` row accumulation, and leases Krylov vectors from
/// [`crate::kernels::reuse::global_pool`]: no entry of the matrix is ever
/// changed, so there is no fill-in. One random projection yields a divisor of
/// the minimal polynomial, and the right one with probability at least `1 -
/// 2n/p`; the result here is the least common multiple over `trials`
/// projections (seeded, so the function is deterministic). `None` when the
/// matrix is not square.
