/// Seeded Gibbs sweeps with a typed conditional sampler taking a zero-based
/// coordinate, normalized state and a uniform draw. No joint log values are
/// recorded. Gibbs sampler driven by user-supplied full conditionals. Each
/// coordinate is refreshed in turn from its full conditional. A conditional is
/// a function of the current state and one uniform variate in `(0, 1)`; it
/// returns the new value of its coordinate, normally by inverting the
/// conditional CDF on a bracketed grid. One sweep over all coordinates is one
/// iteration. [`MhOptions::proposal_sd`] is not used, because Gibbs moves have
/// no proposal distribution; prefer [`gibbs_with_log_posterior`] with
/// [`GibbsOptions`] when you also have the joint log density. Because no joint
/// density is provided, [`Chain::log_posterior`] is filled with `NaN`. # Errors
/// Returns an error when the number of conditionals does not match the state,
/// the state is empty, `n` or `thin` is zero, the iteration budget overflows,
/// or a conditional returns a non-finite value.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_mcmc_gibbs(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_mcmc_gibbs", std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

/// Seeded Gibbs sweeps with a typed coordinate conditional and joint log
/// target. The log posterior is evaluated at every retained draw. Gibbs sampler
/// driven by user-supplied full conditionals that also records the joint
/// `log_posterior` at every kept draw. Each coordinate is refreshed in turn
/// from its full conditional, exactly as in [`gibbs`]. After each retained
/// sweep, `log_posterior(&state)` is evaluated and stored in
/// [`Chain::log_posterior`]. # Errors Returns an error when the number of
/// conditionals does not match the state, the state is empty or contains
/// non-finite values, `n` or `thin` is zero, the iteration budget overflows, a
/// conditional returns a non-finite value, or `log_posterior` returns a
/// non-finite value at a kept draw.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args>
inline Value num_mcmc_gibbs_with_log_posterior(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_mcmc_gibbs_with_log_posterior",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

/// Seeded Hamiltonian Monte Carlo on normalized coordinates with typed
/// log-target and gradient functions and a fixed leapfrog schedule. Hamiltonian
/// Monte Carlo sampler. A standard-normal momentum is drawn at every iteration,
/// the Hamiltonian dynamics of the target are integrated with the leapfrog
/// scheme for `leapfrog_steps` steps of length `step_size`, and the endpoint is
/// accepted with the Metropolis probability `min(1, exp(H_old - H_new))`. The
/// returned chain holds `n` draws taken every `thin` iterations after `burn_in`
/// discarded ones. # Errors Returns an error when the initial state is empty,
/// the step size is not positive and finite, the number of leapfrog steps, `n`
/// or `thin` is zero, the iteration budget overflows, the target log density is
/// not finite at the initial state, or the gradient has the wrong length or a
/// non-finite entry.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_mcmc_hmc(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_mcmc_hmc", std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

/// Seeded Metropolis–Hastings with normalized coordinates, positive Gaussian
/// proposal scales and a typed log-target function. Metropolis-Hastings sampler
/// with a symmetric Gaussian random walk. Each iteration proposes one joint
