/// Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use
/// normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns.
/// Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One
/// classical Runge-Kutta 4 step of `y' = f([t,] y)` as a kernel. `rhs` has
/// `n_state` outputs and either `n_state` inputs (autonomous) or `n_state + 1`
/// with the time as input 0. The step kernel has `n_state` inputs (the state
/// columns of every trajectory), the parameters of `rhs` followed by two more,
/// `t` at index `rhs.params` and the step `h` at `rhs.params + 1`, and
/// `n_state` outputs (the next state). Launching it `steps` times with a
/// changing `t` integrates every row, that is every initial condition, with the
/// same program: the ODE-ensemble pattern. # Errors
/// [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the shape of `rhs` does not match, or
/// when `rhs` is not elementwise or uses `gather` (which addresses columns and
/// cannot be composed).
