/// first axis supplies `t(ρ, s₀)` and the second supplies `t(r₀, σ)`. Their
/// first coordinates define `(r₀, s₀)`. Quadrature uses the sample knots as
/// breakpoints. Targets on a characteristic return the interpolated boundary
/// data. Independent interior targets can be evaluated concurrently and the
/// output order matches the input order. # Errors Returns a shape error for
/// missing or misaligned samples. Domain errors cover nonfinite or unordered
/// data, inconsistent corner values, targets outside `r ≥ r₀ > s ≥ s₀` or the
/// sampled coordinate ranges, and quadrature that cannot produce a finite,
/// converged estimate.
