/// Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape
/// and work/allocation bounds are enforced. P3M reciprocal-space energy, forces
/// and virial with the **optimal (Hockney-Eastwood) influence function** for a
/// general triclinic cell. Charges are assigned with cardinal B-splines of even
/// `order` on a mesh in fractional coordinates; the influence function
/// minimises the rms force error over all charge configurations for `ik`
/// differentiation, `G(k) = sum_m U^2(k_m) (k . k_m) R(k_m) / (k^2 [sum_m
/// U^2(k_m)]^2)` with `R(k) = 4 pi exp(-k^2/4 alpha^2)/k^2`, `U` the transform
/// of the assignment function and the sum running over the `(2 n_alias + 1)^3`
/// aliases `k_m = k + m K b`. The field is obtained by `ik` differentiation of
/// the mesh potential (three inverse FFTs) and interpolated with the assignment
/// function; the virial uses the analytic Ewald reciprocal form with the
/// optimal `G` (exact up to the aliasing error). The self and
/// neutralising-background terms are included. # Errors Fails for a singular
/// cell, an odd or too small spline order, or a mesh smaller than the order.
inline Term num_native_ewald_p3m_reciprocal_cell(const Term &a0, const Term &a1,
                                                 const Term &a2, const Term &a3,
                                                 const Term &a4) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4};
  return apply("num_native_ewald_p3m_reciprocal_cell", args, 5);
}

