/// strengths. The field has one two-component row per original position, with
/// units of source strength divided by length. Evaluates the field in input
/// particle order with new source strengths. # Errors Rejects a wrong source
/// count, non-finite strengths, coincident unsoftened points and fields that
/// are outside the finite range.
inline Term num_native_fmm_evaluate2d(const Term &a0, const Term &a1,
                                      const Term &a2) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2};
  return apply("num_native_fmm_evaluate2d", args, 3);
}

/// Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape
/// and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Adaptive 2-D FMM: the field sum of
/// each source strength times `(x_j - x_i) / (|x_j - x_i|^2 + eps^2)`, with
/// self excluded. Expansions use the unsoftened kernel `1/z`. Interactions
/// closer than `eps / sqrt(theta^(order + 1))` are summed directly so the
/// softening error is bounded by the same scale as the truncation error.
/// Softening comparable to the domain extent can therefore require a quadratic
/// sum. Use [`PreparedFmm2d`] to evaluate new source strengths at fixed
/// positions. # Errors Rejects empty, mismatched or non-finite input, invalid
/// options, coincident unsoftened points and fields that are outside the finite
/// range.
inline Term num_native_fmm_fmm2d(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                                 const Term &a3, const Term &a4) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4};
  return apply("num_native_fmm_fmm2d", args, 5);
}

/// Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape
/// and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Adaptive 3-D FMM for the potential
/// `sum s_j / r` and its gradient field. The P2M, near-field, M2L and L2P
/// passes are parallel over nodes/leaves (each owns its output, so the result
/// is bit-identical to the serial sweep); M2M and L2L are level-sequential and
/// stay serial. # Errors Fails for empty input, length mismatch or `theta`
/// outside `(0, 1)`.
inline Term num_native_fmm_fmm3d(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2,
                                 const Term &a3, const Term &a4) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4};
  return apply("num_native_fmm_fmm3d", args, 5);
}

/// Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape
/// and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Periodic 3-D FMM in a triclinic
/// cell. Evaluates the potential `sum s_j / r` and field `sum s_j (x_j -
/// x_i)/r^3` of charges in the cell `h` (rows are the lattice vectors) with
/// tinfoil boundary conditions and a neutralising background. The central cell
/// and its `(2w+1)^3 - 1` nearest images are summed by the adaptive tree code
/// ([`fmm3d`], Plummer softening `opts.fmm.eps` included); the rest of the
/// lattice enters through the Taylor expansion (degree `2 far_half_order`) of
/// the regularised Ewald lattice potential about the cell centre, combined with
/// the cell's multipole moments. Positions are wrapped into the cell.
/// Self-image interactions are included, the particle's own `n = 0` image is
/// not. # Errors Fails for empty input, mismatched lengths, a singular cell, or
/// invalid FMM options.
inline Term num_native_fmm_periodic_fmm3d(const Term &a0, const Term &a1,
                                          const Term &a2, const Term &a3,
                                          const Term &a4, const Term &a5,
                                          const Term &a6, const Term &a7,
                                          const Term &a8) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8};
  return apply("num_native_fmm_periodic_fmm3d", args, 9);
}

