/// Inclusive bounds use the same dimension as the coordinates. The minimum is
/// finite and nonnegative. A Some upper bound is finite and None is unbounded.
/// The hit record contains physical t and point plus a dimensionless unit
/// normal. Intersects a ray over the inclusive parameter interval `[min_t,
/// max_t]`. The lower bound is finite and nonnegative. The upper bound may be
/// positive infinity. The returned normal follows the vertex winding. Zero
/// directions and rays numerically parallel to the plane have no hit. Near a
/// triangle edge or range endpoint, the signs are checked over the exact
/// binary-float inputs.
