/// Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape
/// and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Wolff single-cluster algorithm:
/// a cluster grown from a random seed spin, each aligned neighbour added with
/// probability `1 - exp(-2/T)`, is flipped as a whole. Rejection-free and free
/// of critical slowing down, so it samples near `T_c` far better than local
/// Metropolis updates. `sweeps` cluster updates are measured after
/// `thermalisation` discarded ones. Runs on the dimension-generic engine
/// [`crate::sim::spin_models::OnModel`] (cold start, periodic `width x height`
/// lattice); the observables are `NaN` for lattices the engine rejects
/// (periodic sides below 3).
