/// Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE
/// values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native
/// interpreter steps. Lowers a tape to a *batch* function that evaluates it at
/// every row. The function's parameters are the input columns (`inputs`
/// slices), the parameter vector (one slice), the output columns (`outputs`
/// slices) and the row count (`I64`): for `row < rows` it stores output `k` of
/// `row` into `out_k[row]`. Missing input elements read NaN, exactly like
/// [`Compiled::call_batch`](super::Compiled::call_batch). Constants and
/// parameters are loop-invariant and evaluated once before the loop. Every row
/// gets the bits [`Tape::eval`](super::tape::Tape::eval) gives it: each tape
/// instruction maps to the LIR instruction with the same IEEE semantics.
/// Returns `None` for tapes with `Gather` (its column is chosen per row, which
/// a column-per-parameter signature cannot express).
