/// Actual native zero-Dirichlet multigrid on its unit interval/cube, mapped to
/// an explicit physical coordinate and solution reference. RHS has
/// solution/coordinate^2 units.1D input contains interior values;2D/3D input
/// includes boundary nodes. Output is flattened in native x-fastest order with
/// explicit shape. Solves `-∇²u = f` on the unit square by running `num_cycles`
/// multigrid V-cycles. Input and output are both flattened with x varying
/// fastest. All boundary values are fixed to zero, and source entries on those
/// boundaries are ignored. With zero cycles, or with a boundary-only 2×2 grid,
