/// dimensions, products/quotients and gradients propagate physical powers;
/// transcendental arguments must be dimensionless. Opaque handles are kind
/// checked, invalid across sessions and after release. Release dependent
/// variables/gradients before their tape. Callbacks scope temporary handles. No
/// native pointer/state is serialized.
inline Term num_native_release(const Term &a0) {
  Term args[] = {a0};
  return apply("num_native_release", args, 1);
}

/// Exact native AD with normalized callback variables and independent physical
/// references: point,positive coordinate_scale,positive
/// value_scale,max_evaluations,callback. Forward callback scalar duals are
/// {val,deriv}; vector duals are {val:vector,deriv:vector}; all dual arithmetic
/// is dimensionless and uses native num_dual_* operators. Reverse callbacks use
/// checked NativeAdVar handles on an ephemeral session tape; native operations
/// enforce same-tape identity and a65536-node limit. Output derivatives restore
/// E/D; no numerical differencing or opaque-callback finite-difference
/// fallback. Exact value and gradient `(f(x), grad f(x))` of `f(&[Var]) -> Var`
/// at `x` in a single reverse-mode pass. # Errors [`AdError::Empty`] when `x`
/// is empty.
