/// evaluation limit. Nelder: x,xscale,yscale,step,tol,iterations,budget,f.
/// Differential evolution:
/// lo,hi,xscale,yscale,population,generations,budget,seed,f. Annealing:
/// x,xscale,yscale,step,temperature,cooling,iterations,budget,seed,f.
/// Constrained:
/// x,xscale,yscale,equality_scale,inequality_scale,tol,iterations,budget,f,eq,ineq.
/// Constraints independently carry C/H units; SQP returns physical multipliers
/// E/C and E/H, native status and second-order verdict. Second-order:
/// x,lambda,mu,xscale,yscale,eqscale,ineqscale,budget,f,eq,ineq. No
/// global-optimality claim; native iteration/status semantics retained.
/// Sequential quadratic programming for `min f(x)` subject to `h(x) = 0` and
/// `g(x) <= 0`. Each iteration linearises the constraints, solves the quadratic
/// program of [`qp_active_set`] for a step `d`, and takes a backtracking step
/// on the `l1` merit function `f + rho (|h|_1 + max(0, g)_1)`. A least-squares
/// restoration phase is run whenever the iterate is infeasible, so the
/// constraints are satisfied to `tol` rather than merely penalised. The
/// multipliers returned in [`ConstrainedResult::lambda`] and
/// [`ConstrainedResult::mu`] are the ones of the final quadratic program, i.e.
/// the exact multipliers of the Lagrangian `L = f + lambda . h + mu . g`; in
/// particular `-mu_i` is the derivative of the optimal value with respect to
/// relaxing `g_i(x) <= 0` to `g_i(x) <= eps`. `grad` may be `None`, in which
/// case central differences are used for the objective; constraint Jacobians
/// are always central differences. Convergence is declared when the violation
/// is at most `tol` and the KKT residual is at most `max(tol, 1e-8)`.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_native_sqp_scaled(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_native_sqp_scaled",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

