/// Native column tape evaluation; each coordinate/output column has independent
/// retained physical references. Evaluates the program at every row of a batch,
/// column-wise. `columns[i][row]` is input `i` (a missing element reads NaN,
/// like a missing input of [`Tape::eval`]); `out[k][row]` receives output `k`
/// for `row < min(out lengths)`. Rows are processed in blocks of
/// [`COLUMN_BLOCK`]: each instruction runs over a whole block before the next
/// one, which turns the per-instruction dispatch of the scalar interpreter into
/// one dispatch per block and lets the arithmetic vectorise. Large pure batches
/// split independent row chunks across the active CPU pool while respecting
/// cancellation and producing the exact same bits as [`Tape::eval`].
