/// Native hyperdual tape Hessian; output(i,j) has units E/(D_i D_j). The
/// Hessian of output `k` with respect to every input at `inputs`, row-major
/// (`n` rows of `n` entries), by hyper-dual arithmetic. Entry `(i, j)` is the
/// `ε₁ε₂` component of a run whose two directions are seeded by `e_i` and
/// `e_j`. Every entry is computed by its own pass, so symmetry is a property of
/// the rules rather than of the assembly. The cost is `n²` forward passes for
/// `n` inputs. Entries are NaN when the tape reaches an opaque operator
/// (`Call`, `Extern1`, `Extern2`) or a domain error; see the module
/// limitations. Large tapes with independent built-in instructions can evaluate
/// rows concurrently in the active CPU pool.
