/// Serial adaptive vector IVP: initial time, final time, initial state vector,
/// absolute state tolerance, relative tolerance, positive finite maximal time
/// step, positive attempt budget, RHS callback. RHS(time,state) returns a
/// same-length vector with state/time dimensions. Returns accepted
/// times/states/evaluations/rejected; the rank-two state tensor has one row per
/// accepted time. Coefficients use coherent units. Callback failures propagate
/// unchanged, rejected attempts consume the budget, and numerical error
/// estimates are heuristic. Events, DAEs and dense-output handles use the
/// native Rust API. Variable-order BDF (orders 1 to 5, NDF coefficients) with a
/// finite-difference Jacobian; see [`bdf_jac`]. # Errors
/// [`OdeError::StepLimit`], [`OdeError::NonFinite`], [`OdeError::SolveFailed`]
/// or [`OdeError::Invalid`].
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_ode_bdf(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_ode_bdf", std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

/// Serial adaptive vector IVP: initial time, final time, initial state vector,
/// absolute state tolerance, relative tolerance, positive finite maximal time
/// step, positive attempt budget, RHS callback. RHS(time,state) returns a
/// same-length vector with state/time dimensions. Returns accepted
/// times/states/evaluations/rejected; the rank-two state tensor has one row per
/// accepted time. Coefficients use coherent units. Callback failures propagate
/// unchanged, rejected attempts consume the budget, and numerical error
/// estimates are heuristic. Events, DAEs and dense-output handles use the
/// native Rust API. Dormand-Prince 5(4) integration of `y' = f(t, y)` from `t0`
/// to `t1` (either direction) with dense output and event detection. `f(t, y,
/// dy)` writes the derivative into `dy`. Events are located by Brent iteration
/// on the continuous extension; a terminal event ends the integration at the
/// event time. # Errors [`OdeError::StepLimit`] or [`OdeError::NonFinite`].
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_ode_dopri5(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_ode_dopri5", std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

/// Dimension-aware adaptive requested-method integration:
/// t0,t1,y0,atol,rtol,h0,h_min,h_max,max_steps,max_evaluations,rhs. Callback
/// derivative has state/time dimensions. Returns accepted times/states/Hermite
/// rates and actual work counters; no method substitution. Adaptive
/// state-dependent stepping does not preserve fixed-step symplecticity.
/// Integrate the selected RK4 or geometric method forward using step doubling.
/// The finite interval uses `start <= end`. The accepted state is two half
/// steps of the requested method, without extrapolation or method substitution.
/// Both the endpoint estimate and the midpoint defect of its cubic Hermite
/// extension control acceptance. A trial needs a representable time strictly
/// between its endpoints. A bracketed event between adjacent times is reported
/// at the later timestamp. Adaptive state-dependent step selection does not
/// retain fixed-step symplecticity. Gauss–Legendre trials reuse stage storage
/// for the duration of the solve. # Errors Invalid inputs or callback outputs,
/// exhausted attempts/evaluations, a tolerance requiring a smaller step than
/// `h_min`, an unsplittable time grid, or failed implicit stages.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_ode_gauss4_adaptive(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_ode_gauss4_adaptive",
                               std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

