/// Compose outer(inner(x)). Inner ordinates must have the dimension of the
/// outer coordinate. The result preserves the inner coordinate scale and the
/// outer ordinate dimension. The maximum result degree is 128. Computes the
/// polynomial composition $P(\\text{inner}(x))$ where `self` is $P$. The
/// arithmetic runs in double-double and the result is rounded to `f64` once, at
