/// Adaptive stochastic path with exact declared callback dimensions and finite
/// budgets. Arguments: t0,t1,positive reference_time,y0,state
/// atol,dimensionless rtol,positive finest cells,proposal/path step
/// budget,callback budget,nonnegative u64 seed,method code 0..9; general
/// variants then take noise count and commutative Bool. Levy variants next take
/// alpha,beta and use dimensionless stable noise at the reference-time scale
/// (diffusion has state units). Jump variants next take intensity (inverse
/// time),dimensionless constant mark vector with independent extent M, then
/// drift,diffusion,jump callbacks sharing that M; other families finish with
/// drift,diffusion callbacks. Brownian diffusion has state/sqrt(time) units.
/// Method codes follow SdeMethod declaration order. Rejections reuse a bounded
/// dyadic noise realization; resolution or work exhaustion is an error. Stable
/// alpha<2 supports only Ito Euler/implicit Euler/theta, while alpha=2 uses the
/// correctly scaled Brownian schemes. Jump times/marks are fixed before
/// rejection and continuous segments stop exactly at each arrival. Local error
/// estimates are heuristic, not global certificates. Integrates a
/// jump-diffusion SDE `dX_t = a(t, X_{t-}) dt + G(t, X_{t-}) dW_t +
/// \\sum_{q=1}^{dN_t} c(t, X_{t-}, Z_q)` over a uniform step grid specified in
/// `options`. * `drift(t, y)` returns the drift vector `a(t, y) in R^n`. *
/// `diffusion(t, y)` returns the diffusion coefficients (`n` for `Diagonal`, `n
