/// Computes sample autocorrelations at lags from zero through `max_lag`.
/// Divides each biased sample autocovariance by the lag-zero autocovariance.
/// The lag-zero result is one. Input scaling cancels before the division, so
/// the correlation remains computable when the variance itself would overflow
/// or underflow. # Errors Returns an error for empty or non-finite samples, a
/// lag at least as large as the sample count, a constant series, or an
/// unrepresentable work extent.
