/// Validated portable native dense/sparse factor definition. Reconstructs
/// native factors from finite defining matrices, preserving method identity and
/// right-hand-side/matrix quotient units. Format/version/kind, CSR sorting,
/// shapes, indices, exact permutations and allocation budgets are checked
/// before native methods. No process-local factor pointers are serialized.
/// IC(0) factorisation `A ≈ L D L^T` (incomplete Cholesky without fill). The
/// lower triangular factor uses the strictly lower pattern of `A`; the upper
/// triangle of `A` is ignored, so the matrix must be symmetric and positive
/// definite for `M = L D L^T` to be a valid CG preconditioner. On a symmetric
/// matrix this is the same operator as [`Csr::ilu0`] written as `L D L^T`
/// instead of `L U`. # Returns `None` for malformed CSR, a missing diagonal, a
/// nonpositive pivot, or unrepresentable lower-triangular factor entries. The
/// factor stores only the strict lower triangle, its transpose and the pivots.
inline Term num_sparse_ic_model_build(const Term &a0) {
  Term args[] = {a0};
  return apply("num_sparse_ic_model_build", args, 1);
}

