/// The regular and irregular Coulomb functions and their derivatives. `F_l(η,
/// ρ)` is the solution regular at the origin and `G_l(η, ρ)` the irregular
/// solution normalised by the Wronskian `F' G - F G' = 1` (so that `G ~ cos θ`
/// at large `ρ`). The dimensionless variables are the Sommerfeld parameter `η`
/// and `ρ = k r`; `l ≥ 0` is the integer angular momentum. The result is `None`
/// outside the domain of the implemented representations (`ρ ≤ 0`, non-finite
/// arguments, `|η| > 10⁶`, `l > 64`, or `24 < ρ ≤ 34` outside the classically
/// allowed region), and also when Steed's fraction fails to certify the
/// physical solution. References: DLMF §§33.2, 33.8 and 33.11; the series is
/// evaluated in double-double arithmetic beyond `ρ = 3` to defeat the `e^{2ρ}`
/// cancellation.
