/// Solves a normalized nonlinear program with bounded typed evaluation and
/// Lagrangian-Hessian callbacks. The evaluation callback receives each
/// consecutive point once. Equality rows precede inequalities g(x) <= 0.
/// Returns KKT residual, convergence, multipliers and callback counts. Solves a
/// sparse nonlinear program by sequential quadratic programming. # Errors
/// Returns an error string when the dimensions reported by the oracle are
/// inconsistent or a working-set system is singular.
///
/// Higher-order: the function parameters are host callbacks.
/// Pass a `Callback` (see `rssn/callback.hpp`) or a `Value` for each
/// one; the result is a `Value`, not a `Term`.
template <class... Args> inline Value num_sqp_solve(Args &&...args) {
  return detail::call_inferred("num_sqp_solve", std::forward<Args>(args)...);
}

