inline Term pi() { return apply("pi", nullptr, 0); }

/// `pid_tune(num, den, rule, lambda)`: `list(kp, ki, kd)` from a
/// first-order-plus-dead-time model of the plant; `rule` is `ziegler_nichols`,
/// `cohen_coon`, `imc`, `amigo` or `chien_hrones_reswick`. Tunes a PID
/// controller for `plant` with the selected rule. `lambda` is the closed-loop
/// time constant of the IMC rule; it is ignored by the other rules and defaults
/// to `max(0.1 tau, theta)`. # Errors Returns an error when the plant step
/// response does not identify a finite first-order-plus-dead-time model or when
/// `lambda` is not positive.
