/// `polylog(s, z)`: polylogarithm `Li_s(z) = sum_{k=1}^infty z^k / k^s`. The
/// polylogarithm `Li_s(z)` for real `s` and real `z`. Real on `z <= 1`
/// (including the negative axis); for `z > 1` the principal value is complex in
/// general and `NaN` is returned, except for non-positive integer `s`, where
/// `Li_{-n}(z)` is the real rational function `z A_n(z)/(1-z)^(n+1)`. At `z =
/// 1` the analytic continuation `ζ(s)` is returned (and `+∞` at the pole `s =
/// 1`).
inline Term polylog(const Term &a0, const Term &a1) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1};
  return apply("polylog", args, 2);
}

/// `polylog_complex(s, re, im)`: `list(re, im)` of `Li_s(z)`. The polylogarithm
/// `Li_s(z)` for complex `s` and `z`, on the principal branch (cut along `[1,
/// ∞)`). * `|z| <= 1/2`: the defining power series; * non-positive integer `s =
/// -n`: the rational function `z A_n(z)/(1-z)^(n+1)` with Eulerian numbers
/// `A_n`; * positive integer `s`: the logarithmic (Bernoulli/Hurwitz)
/// continuation for `|z| <= 3/2` and Kummer's inversion relation beyond, so
/// every `z` is covered; * real `s >= -15.5` and real `z < 1` outside the
/// series' fast region: the same continuation as [`lerch`] with `a = 1`; *
/// other `s`: the logarithmic expansion about `z = 1` for `|ln z| < 4.5` (the
/// expansion is valid for `|ln z| < 2π`, but `ζ(s-k)` overflows `f64` before it
/// converges near that bound); * `z = 1`: `ζ(s)` (the analytic continuation, as
/// in `mpmath`). Outside the stated domain the result is `NaN + NaN i`.
/// Accuracy is about `1e-13` for moderate parameters.
inline Term polylog_complex(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2};
  return apply("polylog_complex", args, 3);
}

