/// `qr_pivoted_diagonal(a)`: non-increasing absolute diagonal `|R_ii|` from
/// column-pivoted QR of `a`. Column-pivoted Householder QR (Businger and
/// Golub). At each step the remaining column of largest norm is brought
/// forward, so the diagonal of `R` decreases in magnitude and its decay reveals
/// the numerical rank. Column norms are downdated and recomputed when
/// cancellation makes the downdate unreliable. Each reflector applies to
/// contiguous columns, with large independent column batches running in
/// parallel. # Errors [`LowRankError::Shape`] for inconsistent storage or
/// non-finite entries, and [`LowRankError::NoConvergence`] if the resulting
/// factor exceeds the representable floating-point range.
inline Term qr_pivoted_diagonal(const Term &a0) {
  Term args[] = {a0};
  return apply("qr_pivoted_diagonal", args, 1);
}

