/// `tt_dense(cores)`: reconstruct dense tensor from a list of tensor-train
/// cores. Dense conversion with an explicit limit on the output element count.
/// Use this when loading cores supplied by another process or when the logical
/// tensor may be exponentially larger than its compressed storage. # Errors
/// Returns an error when size exceeds the limit, allocation fails, or
/// arithmetic overflows.
inline Term tt_dense(const Term &a0) {
  Term args[] = {a0};
  return apply("tt_dense", args, 1);
}

/// `tt_svd(t, tol, max_rank)`: tensor-train SVD of `t` returning `list(cores,
/// error)`. Compress a finite, nonempty dense tensor with TT-SVD. Each split is
/// assigned relative tolerance / sqrt(order - 1). A rank cap may prevent
/// satisfying that tolerance; inspect `tolerance_met` and the returned
/// truncation estimate. Zero tensors use bond rank one. A one-mode tensor is
/// stored exactly. Input is normalized before decomposition to avoid squaring
/// the input's scale in intermediate norm computations. # Errors Returns an
/// error for invalid shape/options, non-finite input, SVD failure,
/// allocation/size overflow or unrepresentable rescaling.
inline Term tt_svd(const Term &a0, const Term &a1, const Term &a2) {
  Term args[] = {a0, a1, a2};
  return apply("tt_svd", args, 3);
}

